/* book exam traps: An amplifier is not a regenerator: it restores power but not pulse shape, so dispersion and jitter pass straight through. | Noise adds up: N identical amplifiers lower the OSNR by 10 log₁₀ N, so 8 amplifiers cost 9.03 dB, not 8 times one amplifier’s penalty. | PCE cannot reach 100 percent: with a 980 nm pump and a 1550 nm signal the ceiling is 980/1550 = 63.2 percent, because each signal photon carries less energy than a pump photon. | The EDFA C-band is 1530 to 1565 nm, not the whole low-loss window from 1260 to 1625 nm. | An SOA facet without its anti-reflection coating gives feedback, and the chip lases instead of amplifying. */
