/* book: lead: At high power the refractive index of silica rises with the light intensity. A pulse then changes its own phase as it travels, a chirp that widens its spectrum: self-phase modulation (SPM). When the fiber has anomalous dispersion, that chirp can cancel the dispersion broadening exactly, and the pulse travels unchanged as a soliton. Only a few syllabi teach this topic. SPM sets the power ceiling of */
