/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Silica is not perfectly linear.
   - The intensity is not uniform across the mode, so one number, the effective area Aeff, stands for the mode size (about 80 µm² in standard single-mode fiber).
   - A lossy fiber weakens the light as it goes, so the nonlinearity acts over an effective length Leff = (1 − e−αL)/α, with α the loss in 1/km (α = loss in dB/km ÷ 4.343).
   - A pulse carries its own index change, so it phase-modulates itself.
   - This is the practical limit on power per WDM channel.
   - With dispersion the pulse envelope A(z,T) obeys the nonlinear Schrödinger equation (NLS): ∂A/∂z + (α/2)A + (iβ₂/2)∂²A/∂T² = iγ|A|²A.
   - Two lengths compete.
*/
