/* book Worked example 2: Q: A standard fiber has n₂ = 2.6 × 10⁻²⁰ m²/W, Aeff = 80 µm² and a loss of 0.2 dB/km at 1550 nm. One WDM channel of 10 mW is launched into an 80 km span. Find γ, Leff, the peak SPM phase and the power at which this phase reaches 1 rad.
   1. γ = 2πn₂/(λAeff) = 2π × 2.6 × 10⁻²⁰ ÷ (1550 × 10⁻⁹ × 80 × 10⁻¹²) = 1.317 × 10⁻³ W⁻¹m⁻¹ = 1.32 W⁻¹km⁻¹.
   2. α = 0.2/4.343 = 0.0461 km⁻¹, so αL = 0.0461 × 80 = 3.68 and e−3.68 = 0.0251. Leff = (1 − 0.0251)/0.0461 = 21.17 km.
   3. φNL = γP Leff = 1.317 × 0.010 × 21.17 = 0.279 rad.
   4. For 1 rad: P = 1/(γLeff) = 1/(1.317 × 21.17) = 0.0359 W = 35.9 mW.
   5. Check: LNL = 1/(γP) = 1/(1.317 × 0.010) = 75.9 km at 10 mW, much longer than Leff, so SPM in one span is weak at this power.
   Answer: γ = 1.32 W⁻¹km⁻¹, Leff = 21.17 km, φNL = 0.279 rad at 10 mW, and the phase reaches 1 rad at about 35.9 mW. */
