/* book exam traps: Using average power in γP₀ instead of the peak power P₀. For a short pulse the average power is much smaller, so the nonlinearity is badly underestimated. | Forgetting the sign of β₂. A bright soliton needs anomalous dispersion, β₂ < 0; with normal dispersion the SPM chirp and the dispersion chirp add and the pulse spreads faster. | Writing z₀ = LD. The soliton period is (π/2)LD, about 1.571 LD, and it is the period of the higher-order solitons; the fundamental soliton never changes shape. | Putting λ in nm or Aeff in µm² into γ = 2πn₂/(λAeff) without converting. Use metres, then multiply W⁻¹m⁻¹ by 1000 for W⁻¹km⁻¹. */
